              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Arabic for to knit, then the Arabic for to sew."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: نرد",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نرد — nard — \"dice\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "رمى أخي النرد وفاز. ramā akhī an-nard wa-fāza. My brother threw the dice and won."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "نرد (nard) was borrowed from Persian: it is a Persian word, arabicized, for the game of backgammon and its pieces (Lane). Today it names the dice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
